**C++ Function to Manipulate Forward List of Strings:**
```cpp
void insertAfterTarget(forward_list<string>& list, const string& target, const string& newStr) {
  auto it = list.begin();
  while (it != list.end() && *it != target) {
    ++it;
  }
  if (it == list.end()) {
    list.push_back(newStr);
  } else {
    it->push_back(' ');
    it->append(newStr);
  }
}
```
Note: The C++ function assumes that the forward list is maintained in a thread-safe manner.']

